# text_id = 1666
# text = Although there has been a gradual decline in the number of Welsh speakers since the census of 1911 — when , incidentally , they amounted to nearly 1 million — much of it has been due to emigration to England , where many of them have tried , and in cases have succeeded , to retain their Welsh nationality and language .
