# text_id = 1843
# text = It is true that these duties , when originally introduced in 1961 by the then Chancellor of the Exchequer , were said by him to be on revenue grounds , but , in fact , Ministers in the last Government made it clear that they were being retained both for revenue purposes and for protection of the coal industry .
