# text_id = 1921
# text = The Lord Chancellor , in his circular to advisory committees , has said that he cannot emphasise too often or too emphatically that the first and much the most important consideration in the selection and appointment of justices is that the candidate should be personally suitable on points of character , integrity and understanding and should be generally recognised as such by those among whom they live and work .
