# text_id = 1933
# text = One was that the fact that a large number of people had been returned to some kind of home , and therefore had left the camps , had had a most stimulating effect upon the refugees in the camps ; it made them feel less apathetic than they were , and made them easier to rehabilitate and , to a certain extent , more willing to co-operate in their own resettlement .
