# text = But it is the particular task of the information officer and his staff not only to be able to present our policies in every field realistically and convincingly to his contacts , but to seek positively for useful outlets for the dissemination of British views through all the media of communication in the country where he is stationed , selecting whichever method seems to him most appropriate in the circumstances .
