# text_id = 1956
# text = The Government will find it very difficult to defend a situation in which a person paying 1s . or 2s . a week on a life policy has imposed upon him a Capital Gains Tax of 35 per cent . or 40 per cent. , whereas normally as individuals such persons would either pay no Capital Gains Tax at all or would pay at a much lower rate than this .
