# text_id = 1962
# text = In this general argument about the independent deterrent there has been often put forward by the " theologians " of the subject — and we live in a world of " theology " on the deterrent — the idea that the possession of the deterrent by one independent Power is apt to be used as a catalyst by that Power for drawing to itself wider powers for its own defence .
