# text_id = 2000
# text = The basic argument which tie unit and investment trust movements advanced in objection to the whole basis of taxation which is envisaged — is the argument on principle , which is that it is quite absurd that people who invest — and they are usually , inevitably , small savers — in unit and investment trusts should be penalised and charged a higher rate of tax than if they invested direct .
