# text_id = 2011
# text = The noble Viscount , Lord Eccles , drew attention to the rather surprising amount of power or influence which the Government are seeking to exercise , without , as it would appear , having any means other than the threat of taking over a library authority , or of making public complaints about it , or by giving general encouragement , of pressing local authorities to bring up their standards .
