# text_id = 2044
# text = At Question Time on March 4 the noble Earl , Lord Alexander of Hillsborough , who leads the Opposition , expressed grave misgivings about the fact that the main bodies in the trade had not been consulted before the Agreement was drawn up , and also about the failure of the Government to publish the terms of the Agreement , or even to make them available to Parliament until recently .
