# text_id = 2077
# text = I believe that it was Lord Eccles who , when he was Minister of Education , appealed to parents in this country , some of whom are going to considerable trouble and expense to get their children to private fee- paying primary schools , to send them to county maintained and aided schools from the age of five , at least until the age of nine , if not eleven .
