# text_id = 2103
# text = There was a voluntary survey made some months ago in Tonbridge , and it worked out that approximately 60 per cent . of the persons who were taking their cars to their railway station did so because their bus services were inadequate , or because they were so badly timed that the commuters would find considerable delay , either in catching their train , or in returning home in the evening .
