# text_id = 2137
# text = The question of the Oder - Neisse line was not mentioned by the Prime Minister , and yet anybody who knows anything about the fears of the Eastern Europeans recognises that the anxiety that the Poles and the Czechs have about the feeling of the Germans that they must get back to their pre-war frontiers is one of the greatest forces which keep the Eastern countries under the Russian umbrella .
