# text_id = 2147
# text = I submit that when it is merely an option for the tenant to determine a lease and when the landlord , the person on whom the premium is charged to tax , is bound to allow the lease to run over the 50 years , it should be treated as a lease for a period exceeding 50 years , a lease the premium for which is not chargeable to tax .
