# text_id = 2161
# text = This , too , would manifestly be of particular importance to those in civil or military employment who retire relatively early , since it stands to reason that among the pre-1956 pensioners there must , on the whole , be more who are Service pensioners or pensioners from employments with an early retirement age than from employments where it is normal to retire at the age of 60 or after .
